WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:08.170
Netflix's Stranger Things has captivated audiences
with a satisfying throwback to classic '80s

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:12.629
paranormal thrillers But how'd this modern
classic actually happen?

00:00:12.629 --> 00:00:17.190
Here's a look at the untold truth of Stranger
Things.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.820
Super Duffer Brothers

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.320
Twins Matt and Ross Duffer, the writer-director
duo who created the show, showed an early

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.830
interest in filmmaking, experimenting with
home movies as early as third grade.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.480
They pursued their passion by studying film
at Chapman University.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.320
Their first movie was Hidden, a horror film
which didn't receive wide release.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.960
But it did catch the eye of M. Night Shyamalan,
who hired them to work on his series Wayward

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:45.960
Pines.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.520
That experience gave the Duffers the start
they needed to pitch their own series.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:56.550
With the help of producers Dan Cohen and Shawn
Levy, Netflix eventually bought the show—but

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:01.559
only after it was rejected by at least 15
other networks.

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:03.050
Strong Island

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.950
Stranger Things takes place in Hawkins, Indiana.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:11.760
But the Duffers originally wanted to play
with the concept of a waterside setting—specifically

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.720
Montauk, New York.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:19.080
The region's real-life history may have inspired
their story: legend has it that the town's

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:26.440
Camp Hero Air Force Base was a lot like MKUltra
in very disturbing ways, including serving

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:32.490
as the site of rumored government experiments
with mind control on kidnapped children.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.430
Georgia On My Mind

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:40.030
Stranger Things was filmed in the Atlanta,
Georgia area, which is also home to a number

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:45.590
of television and film productions, so there
was just bound to be a location crossover

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.040
or two.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.970
The Bellwood Quarry, where fake-Will's body
is found and Mike is bullied into cliff-diving,

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:58.790
was the same site seen in The Walking Dead's
first season and The Hunger Games movies.

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:03.680
Your next Hollywood-inspired trip destination
has just been booked.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.970
Font Of Wisdom

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:09.899
Most of Stranger Things' pop culture references
were put in on purpose, and the title art

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:12.220
font is no exception.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:17.951
It's an altered version of Benguiat, which
was used on a slew of classic Stephen King

00:02:17.951 --> 00:02:24.750
book covers—including but not limited to
Cujo, Salem's Lot, Firestarter, Pet Sematary,

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.630
Misery, and The Stand.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:33.090
The typeface, which was designed by Ed Benguiat,
was also popularized in 1978, and also has

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:39.910
been seen in the openings for films like Star
Trek Generations and Star Trek: First Contact.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.170
'80s cinema school

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:47.190
Finding the right child star for Stranger
Things was important, because even though

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:52.280
there are cast members with higher billing,
the show's heart revolves around the kids.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:03:00.000
The Duffers auditioned 906 boys and 307 girls
for the roles using scenes from Stand By Me.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.320
When they finally settled on the cast, they
were sent home with instructions to watch

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.440
films like Poltergeist and The Goonies to
get a sense of the look and feel of the show

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.540
to come.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.450
Clearly it paid off.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:16.989
On the first day of filming, they shot the
first Dungeons and Dragons session that starts

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:17.989
the series.

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.640
The Duffers told Entertainment Weekly:

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:24.739
"Our boys flew through the scene effortlessly
and energetically, and their chemistry was

00:03:24.739 --> 00:03:28.459
electric; they felt like they had known each
other their whole lives.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:34.099
Other than when we sold the show to Netflix,
this was the single biggest moment for Stranger

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:35.099
Things."

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:36.420
Buzzcut, Baby

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:41.890
Millie Bobby Brown, who turned in stunning
work as the superpowered Eleven, didn't know

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:46.209
she'd have to shear off her locks until she'd
already won the role.

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:51.260
She eventually came around to the idea after
being shown an image of Charlize Theron's

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.690
buzzcut in Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:59.350
She was also encouraged by an old pic of co-star
Winona Ryder, who'd sported a pixie cut in

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.350
her younger days.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:01.350
"Sort of a choice-"

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.350
"And I showed you my school picture."

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:07.959
"And Winona showed me-so I thought like, ya
know Winona looked cool back in the day with

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:11.989
ya know the pixie cut, and I thought, maybe
I could bring it back?"

00:04:11.989 --> 00:04:13.190
Channeling Meryl Streep

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:19.360
Winona Ryder, a legend of the '80s herself
thanks to Heathers and Beetlejuice, was one

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.379
of the first casting picks for Stranger Things.

00:04:22.379 --> 00:04:27.360
But when she was approached about the show,
she had no idea what streaming was, and little

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.939
TV experience.

00:04:28.939 --> 00:04:33.419
For her character's look, though, she found
inspiration in Meryl Streep's performance

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:37.430
in Silkwood, which was released the same year
as the show's events.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:43.110
Her hair in the show was something of a tribute
to the Oscar-winning star.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.039
Stephen King is a fan

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:50.389
As one of the biggest inspirations for Stranger
Things, author Stephen King's praise of the

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:52.660
show is worth a lot.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.770
The author wrote on Twitter that when he watched
the show it was like "watching Steve King's

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:04.300
Greatest Hits … in a good way," and graded
the program an A for "pure fun."

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:09.849
Interestingly enough, Finn Wolfhard, who plays
Mike Wheeler in the show, will star in another

00:05:09.849 --> 00:05:16.659
big Stephen King-inspired property: the upcoming
big-screen adaptation of IT, which—full

00:05:16.659 --> 00:05:21.229
circle!—the Duffers tried in vain to direct
years ago.

00:05:21.229 --> 00:05:22.229
Thanks for watching!

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:26.199
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:30.380
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you want to see in Stranger Things, season

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:30.399
two…

